(window.LEARN_C = window.LEARN_C || {})["mth-12-07"] = {"7.1":{"s":"A linear inequation in two variables, such as ax + by ≤ c, is shown on the XY plane by shading one side of the line ax + by = c: a half plane. To pick the side, test a point such as the origin: if it satisfies the inequality, shade its side. The common shaded region of several inequalities is their solution set. A convex set is one where the segment joining any two of its points stays inside.","w":["Test the origin only if the line does not pass through it; otherwise test another point.","x ≥ 0 and y ≥ 0 limit the region to the first quadrant."]},"7.2":{"s":"A linear programming problem asks for the largest or smallest value of a linear objective function, such as a profit or a cost, subject to linear constraints and x, y ≥ 0. Formulate it from the word problem, draw the feasible region, and find its corner points. When the feasible region is bounded, the best value of the objective function is reached at a corner point: compute it at each corner and compare.","w":["Name the unknowns first, then write the objective function and each constraint from the table of data.","For a bounded feasible region, the maximum and minimum are found among its corner points."]}};
